cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper and this archived release."
title: "LROT: ligand-receptor-guided optimal transport for spatial transcriptomics slice alignment"
abstract: "Reference implementation of LROT, which embeds a ligand-receptor communication prior as a third cost channel in an entropy-regularised fused Gromov-Wasserstein framework for spatial transcriptomics section alignment, together with the scripts and intermediate results needed to reproduce the figures of the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "LROT authors"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.4"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zly36/LROT"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22915948"
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - optimal transport
  - Gromov-Wasserstein
  - ligand-receptor
  - section alignment
  - 3D reconstruction
